From 0d9d22efae4638e7f8ae520e8f577a64146de820 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:28:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add XPU support to FBGEMM sparse and jagged ops tests

Add XPU device support to misc_ops_test.py and permute_sparse_features_test.py.
Includes support for permute_1D_sparse_data and permute_2D_sparse_data operators.
Also adds XPU support to test_asynchronous_complete_cumsum_2d in cumsum_test.py.
Adds XPU support to block_bucketize_test.py for the block_bucketize_sparse_features
and block_bucketize_sparse_features_inference operators.
Adds XPU support to reorder_batched_test.py for the reorder_batched_ad_lengths
and reorder_batched_ad_indices operators.
Adds XPU support to jagged/jagged_index_select_2d_test.py for the
jagged_index_select_2d_forward operator; the backward + opcheck sections are
skipped on XPU because only the forward kernel has an XPU implementation.

Adds XPU support to the jagged tensor operator tests so the SYCL/XPU
implementations are exercised against FBGEMM's reference results:

- jagged/2d_to_dense_test.py: jagged_2d_to_dense (forward + truncation cases).
- jagged/dense_to_jagged_test.py: dense_to_jagged / dense_to_jagged_forward
  round-trip.
- jagged/jagged_to_padded_dense_test.py: jagged_to_padded_dense[_forward].
- jagged/elementwise_binary_test.py:
  jagged_dense_elementwise_add_jagged_output (the plain add / mul variants stay
  CPU/CUDA only).

These jagged ops implement both forward and backward, so their backward,
gradcheck and opcheck sections run on XPU as they do on CPU/CUDA.

Signed-off-by: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
Co-authored-by: Felipe Leza Alvarez <felipe.leza.alvarez@intel.com>
